       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. 15 g/day of acetaminophen has no therapeutic use. It's well into the range that causes acute liver failure, and a single 5 g dose is already above the maximum for one administration. Normal liver function and a 70 kg weight don't make it safe.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a standard dose right away.** For example, 1,000 mg PO three times daily (3 g/day), or up to 1,000 mg four times daily (4 g/day maximum).\n- **Enter the order with a different dose or frequency** if you had a specific target in mind.\n- **Help with a different problem.** If this was meant to treat severe pain or fever that isn't responding, I can enter a multimodal regimen with other agents, as you direct.\n\nIf you think there is a reason for this dose, I'd suggest talking with pharmacy or toxicology before it goes into the system. Tell me which of these you'd like."
      }
